course: dictionary
lesson: 11668
title: Assessment: a test or a judgement
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An assessment is a way of finding out what someone knows or can do. Often it is a test, a quiz or marked work. «Our class has an assessment on fractions on Friday.» Fractions and a Friday test tell you that an assessment here means a test.
explain: The word also means a careful judgement about something, such as how big a risk is or how much damage was done. «The workers did a risk assessment before they climbed the tower.» They thought carefully about the dangers before they started.
explain: A good check is to swap in your meaning. «The vet made an assessment of the injured bird.» If you put "judgement" in place of assessment, the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An assessment is a test or task to find out what someone knows or can do.
fact: An assessment can also be a careful judgement about a situation, a risk or a value.
fact: «End-of-unit assessment» means a test at the end of a topic.
fact: «Risk assessment» means checking the dangers before a trip or an activity.
fact: «Assessment of damage» means judging how much harm was done, for example after a storm.
exercise: «Our class has a spelling assessment on Monday.» What is an assessment here? | A holiday trip to the zoo | *A test to find out what you know | A new pencil case | A loud noise in the hall
exercise: «Before the school trip, the teacher did a risk assessment.» What was she checking? | The names of the cooks | The colour of the bus | *The dangers of the trip | How many sandwiches to bring
exercise: Which phrase means judging how much harm a storm caused? | End-of-unit quiz | Risk assessment | Spelling test | *Assessment of damage
test: «The end-of-unit assessment covers all the maths we did this term.» What does end-of-unit assessment mean? | A book about maths | Walk to the end of the road | Party at the end of term | *A test at the end of a topic
test: In «The vet made an assessment of the injured bird», which word could replace assessment with almost the same meaning? | *Judgement | Puddle | Holiday | Song
exam: Mia says, «An assessment is just a boring test.» What is the best answer? | Only doctors do assessments | Yes, it is always a test in class | No, it is a kind of cake | *Not always: it can also be a careful judgement about a risk or a value
